    "captured": "2026-08-17",
    "why_not_utls": "uTLS has no table for this build. At upstream commit 23b1dac1 (2026-08-02) HelloChrome_Auto is still HelloChrome_133 and no uTLS table anywhere carries the ML-DSA signature algorithms Chromium now offers, so transcribing uTLS would reproduce a hello no shipping Chrome sends.",
    "capture_note": "First-party capture. The browser was driven headlessly on the maintainer's machine against a local listener that recorded the raw ClientHello record, and the same browser was driven again through a recording CONNECT relay to a public destination; both hellos produced the identical JA4, so the localhost capture is the hello this build sends to the internet and not a loopback special case.",
    "verified_against_live_browser": true,
    "verified_against_live_reality_server": false,
    "measured_ja4": "t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_806a8c22fdea",
    "measured_ja4_note": "JA4 of the captured hello, and of three further hellos the same browser sent to a public destination through a recording relay -- all four identical. The computation producing it was validated against tls.browserleaks.com on a Firefox capture, hash and raw form both, character for character. chrome_133 reads t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_d8a2da3f94cd: JA4_a and JA4_b already match, and JA4_c is where the ML-DSA schemes land."
  },
